"text": "In Spain, the plan now depended on a chain of strangers. On May 1st, two Spanish doctors carried out a post-mortem in Huelva, with the British vice-consul present. As the heat of the day rose, Haselden suggested that the doctors might like to finish up and go to lunch. They agreed, and recorded the cause of death as asphyxiation through immersion in the sea.",
